<%# HAND A PENDING CART BACK TO THE CONTEST PAGE.
    A visitor who built a lineup and then left to sign in — the Google full-page
    redirect, the new-signup token purchase — is on their way BACK to finish an
    entry, and the saved cart is only replayed by the board on the contest page
    (selectionBoard#init in _turf_totals_board). Two pages they can land on
    instead render no board:

      * the live board (contest: given), where /contests/:id sends a visitor
        once a game has started; it hands back only a cart for its own contest;
      * the root lobby (contest: nil), where every sign-in with no destination
        lands; it hands back a cart for whichever contest it names.

    Landing on either would leave them signed in with no entry and nothing
    saying why. Same key and same 30-minute freshness as the board's init, and
    the item is LEFT IN PLACE: the board consumes it. The contest page never
    routes, so this cannot loop. ONE hand-off per saved cart (handedOff): the
    contest page renders no board for a visitor who already holds an entry, so
    nothing consumes the cart there, and an unmarked one would pull them off
    this page for the full 30 minutes. %>
<% contest = local_assigns[:contest] %>
<script>
  (function () {
    try {
      var parsed = JSON.parse(localStorage.getItem('pendingContestEntry') || 'null');
      var fresh = parsed && parsed.savedAt && (Date.now() - parsed.savedAt) < (30 * 60 * 1000);
      if (!fresh || parsed.handedOff) return;
<% if contest %>
      if (parsed.contestSlug === <%= raw contest.slug.to_json %>) {
        parsed.handedOff = true;
        localStorage.setItem('pendingContestEntry', JSON.stringify(parsed));
        window.location.replace(<%= raw contest_page_path(contest).to_json %>);
      }
<% else %>
      if (typeof parsed.contestSlug === 'string' && parsed.contestSlug) {
        parsed.handedOff = true;
        localStorage.setItem('pendingContestEntry', JSON.stringify(parsed));
        window.location.replace('/contests/' + encodeURIComponent(parsed.contestSlug) + '/contest');
      }
<% end %>
    } catch (e) { /* bad JSON or storage unavailable: stay on this page */ }
  })();
</script>
